<!--
  RUT_MortuaryCrawler.xml                UtinniPatches - COMMISSION_LEDGER_CLEANUP_1

  Resolves ledger slug
  `the_scarlands:mortuary-guild-carrion-specialist-dedicated-body`
  (design/Jawa/worldbuilding/biomes/the_scarlands.md §4: "The Mortuary Guild
  — slow, patient carrion-specialists, the only things that can digest the
  preserved dead of a graveyard that won't properly rot. Uncannily calm
  where everything else is mad; the one safe animal here, and the most
  disturbing"; roster's own new_defs entry, rosters/the_scarlands.json,
  mechanic_load "none blocking; AA_Helixien is the interim body").

  A genuinely NEW body, not a reskin of the interim. Checked cast_assignment.csv
  first (per this item's own "watch out"): AA_Helixien is already an
  intentionally shared, multi-homed "corpse decayer special" cast across
  FIVE biomes (RUT_Contagion/Miasma/PoisonForest/Scarlands/Slime, all
  "keep"/"adjust-keep") — reusing its own asset again under a new defName
  would only add a sixth instance of the same shared reuse, not give
  Scarlands the dedicated species this roster row actually asks for. No
  other unclaimed "slow calm scavenger" body exists in the live cast for
  this biome (checked). The only candidate donor found, `BMT_CarrionVulture`
  (Biomes! Polluted Lands), is `dormant` in animal_census.csv — its mod is
  not in the active list, so per the GR_Paraceramuffalo precedent
  (COMMISSION_LEDGER_CLEANUP_1 wave 1, desert sheet) its texPath is not a
  live asset to reuse, only a scale/flavor reference (a flying vulture-
  analog, used here only to confirm "carrion specialist, calm" as a
  plausible silhouette family) — so this is authored from scratch with new
  art, same posture RUT_FleetFlier (the_forge wave) used when no live donor
  passed.

  Mechanism: "digests the preserved dead" needs no bespoke C# — ordinary
  foodType Carnivore + predator=false is the same vanilla combination
  RimWorld's own scavenger-type wildlife (non-hunting carrion eaters) already
  uses; nothing in the sheet's own "engine feasibility pass owed" list names
  this creature, matching the roster's own "none blocking" tag exactly.
  manhunterOnDamageChance/OnTameFailChance are zeroed and wildness kept low
  deliberately — the sheet's own text ("the one safe animal here") is read
  as a real mechanical property, the same "flavor text as a real stat"
  discipline RUT_FleetFlier's ComfyTemperatureMax used for "retreat before
  they perish". ComfyTemperatureMin/Max (10/65) match RUT_PyrelandsFauna's
  own extreme-heat-biome precedent — Scarlands' own measured median temp is
  59.4 C (RUT_Scarlands.xml header).

  Label "pallbearer" ruled by owner card 2026-09-24
  (SCARLANDS_SHIPPING_NAMES_1). `RUT_MortuaryCrawler` stays as the internal
  defName by that item's own scope; "Mortuary Guild" in the sheet names the
  GROUP, not the species.

  Art: genuinely new, no existing render found (checked infrastructure/
  artpipe/{done,pending,registry.jsonl} for "mortuary"/"crawler" — clean).
  Three facing jobs filed this pass (south/east/north; west mirrors east) —
  rutmortuarycrawler_v1_{south,east,north}.json.
-->
<Defs>

  <ThingDef ParentName="AnimalThingBase">
    <defName>RUT_MortuaryCrawler</defName>
    <label>pallbearer</label>
    <description>A heavy, armor-plated scavenger that moves at exactly one speed: unhurried. It works a graveyard the way nothing else here can — patiently, methodically, digesting the preserved dead of ground that won't properly rot. Everything else in the Scarlands is one wrong step from madness; the pallbearer never seems to notice there was a war at all, which is exactly what makes it the worst thing to watch eat.</description>
    <statBases>
      <MoveSpeed>1.2</MoveSpeed>
      <Mass>85</Mass>
      <MarketValue>140</MarketValue>
      <Wildness>0.3</Wildness>
      <ComfyTemperatureMin>10</ComfyTemperatureMin>
      <ComfyTemperatureMax>65</ComfyTemperatureMax>
      <ArmorRating_Sharp>0.25</ArmorRating_Sharp>
      <ArmorRating_Blunt>0.15</ArmorRating_Blunt>
    </statBases>
    <tools>
      <li>
        <label>bite</label>
        <capacities>
          <li>Bite</li>
        </capacities>
        <power>9</power>
        <cooldownTime>2.2</cooldownTime>
        <linkedBodyPartsGroup>Teeth</linkedBodyPartsGroup>
        <chanceFactor>0.5</chanceFactor>
      </li>
      <li>
        <label>foreclaw</label>
        <capacities>
          <li>Scratch</li>
        </capacities>
        <power>7</power>
        <cooldownTime>2</cooldownTime>
        <linkedBodyPartsGroup>FrontLeftPaw</linkedBodyPartsGroup>
      </li>
      <li>
        <label>foreclaw</label>
        <capacities>
          <li>Scratch</li>
        </capacities>
        <power>7</power>
        <cooldownTime>2</cooldownTime>
        <linkedBodyPartsGroup>FrontRightPaw</linkedBodyPartsGroup>
      </li>
    </tools>
    <race>
      <body>QuadrupedAnimalWithPawsAndTail</body>
      <predator>false</predator>
      <baseBodySize>2.2</baseBodySize>
      <baseHealthScale>1.3</baseHealthScale>
      <baseHungerRate>0.55</baseHungerRate>
      <foodType>Carnivore</foodType>
      <leatherDef>Leather_Heavy</leatherDef>
      <herdAnimal>false</herdAnimal>
      <roamMtbDays>6</roamMtbDays>
      <trainability>None</trainability>
      <manhunterOnDamageChance>0</manhunterOnDamageChance>
      <manhunterOnTameFailChance>0</manhunterOnTameFailChance>
      <lifeExpectancy>22</lifeExpectancy>
      <gestationPeriodDays>12</gestationPeriodDays>
      <litterSizeCurve>
        <points>
          <li>(0.5, 0)</li>
          <li>(1, 1)</li>
          <li>(1.5, 0.6)</li>
          <li>(2, 0)</li>
        </points>
      </litterSizeCurve>
      <lifeStageAges>
        <li>
          <def>AnimalBaby</def>
          <minAge>0</minAge>
        </li>
        <li>
          <def>AnimalJuvenile</def>
          <minAge>0.2</minAge>
        </li>
        <li>
          <def>AnimalAdult</def>
          <minAge>0.5</minAge>
        </li>
      </lifeStageAges>
      <soundMeleeHitPawn>Pawn_Melee_SmallScratch_HitPawn</soundMeleeHitPawn>
      <soundMeleeHitBuilding>Pawn_Melee_SmallScratch_HitBuilding</soundMeleeHitBuilding>
      <soundMeleeMiss>Pawn_Melee_SmallScratch_Miss</soundMeleeMiss>
      <soundEating>Warg_Eat</soundEating>
    </race>
    <tradeTags>
      <li>AnimalExotic</li>
    </tradeTags>
  </ThingDef>

  <PawnKindDef ParentName="AnimalKindBase">
    <defName>RUT_MortuaryCrawler</defName>
    <label>pallbearer</label>
    <race>RUT_MortuaryCrawler</race>
    <combatPower>60</combatPower>
    <wildGroupSize>1~2</wildGroupSize>
    <ecoSystemWeight>0.6</ecoSystemWeight>
    <lifeStages>
      <li>
        <bodyGraphicData>
          <texPath>Things/Pawn/Animal/RUT_MortuaryCrawler/RUT_MortuaryCrawler</texPath>
          <graphicClass>Graphic_Multi</graphicClass>
          <drawSize>1.0</drawSize>
        </bodyGraphicData>
      </li>
      <li>
        <bodyGraphicData>
          <texPath>Things/Pawn/Animal/RUT_MortuaryCrawler/RUT_MortuaryCrawler</texPath>
          <graphicClass>Graphic_Multi</graphicClass>
          <drawSize>1.6</drawSize>
        </bodyGraphicData>
      </li>
      <li>
        <bodyGraphicData>
          <texPath>Things/Pawn/Animal/RUT_MortuaryCrawler/RUT_MortuaryCrawler</texPath>
          <graphicClass>Graphic_Multi</graphicClass>
          <drawSize>2.2</drawSize>
